# PassOrch environment example for Docker Compose.
#
# Copy to ".env" (git-ignored) and uncomment what you need.  Never put
# real secrets in this file or in any committed file.

# Long random value; when set, state-changing requests require
#   Authorization: Bearer <value>
# Reads stay unauthenticated (documented in README "Authentication").
# PASSORCH_API_TOKEN=

# Guard tuning (generous defaults shown; positive numbers only - counts
# and byte caps are integers, the window may be fractional seconds).
# PASSORCH_RATE_LIMIT=120
# PASSORCH_RATE_WINDOW_SECONDS=60
# PASSORCH_MAX_BODY_BYTES=65536

# Trusted reverse proxies (opt-in, Phase 12B): comma-separated exact IPs
# of proxies the app should key its rate limit behind.  When unset (the
# default) X-Forwarded-For is never consulted and the socket peer is the
# key.  Only valid exact IPs are accepted - hostnames and CIDR ranges
# fail fast at startup.
# PASSORCH_TRUSTED_PROXIES=

# Persistence: compose already sets PASSORCH_JOB_DB=/data/passorch.db
# (the named volume).  Only change this if you mount your own path.
# PASSORCH_JOB_DB=/data/passorch.db
